  "notes": "Standard 16-bar tune from two abcnotation.com ABCs (John Chambers demo, K:C; Lester Bailey, K:G transposed to C); incipit 1-3-4-5 confirmed by hymnary.org. 3-beat pickup C-E-F; each long G is a whole note; bars 2/4/8/12 open with rests as in the source. Old version had no pickup and squashed every long note to a quarter. Range C4-G4. The closing bar is the 1-beat remainder of the pickup bar (a rest, as the source's final 'z'), so the last note (C4 whole) ends at beat 63 of a 64-beat / 16-measure frame."
